 wheelchair and prosthetics are medically necessary** — this is not either/or.\n\n5. **Concurrent Issues Affecting Prosthetic Rehab**:\n- Mild TBI: Attention and balance deficits may slow prosthetic training.\n- PTSD/Depression: Motivation, engagement, and pain tolerance all affected.\n- Phantom pain: Must be adequately managed — severe phantom pain interferes with prosthetic wearing.\n- Hearing loss: Affects balance (vestibular component) and communication during training.',
